<h1 id="executive-summary">1. Executive summary</h1>
<p>The proposed feature converts expensive synchronous ICN actions into
managed background jobs. A user selects documents or folders in Browse
or Search, reviews the source, destination, options and estimated
impact, and submits a request. ICN creates a FileNet BulkRequest custom
object and returns an acknowledgement; a separate worker tier executes
the work in bounded chunks, records checkpoints, and publishes progress
to a dedicated dashboard.</p>
<p>The design supports four request types—copy, move, delete and
restore—through one parent class and four subclasses. The parent
contains common lifecycle, ownership, progress, checkpoint and audit
fields; subclasses add operation-specific fields. FileNet is the durable
request store and lightweight job queue. No separate application
database is required for the baseline solution.</p>
