<h1 id="request-and-processing-flows">5. Request and processing
flows</h1>
<h2 id="submit-flow">5.1 Submit flow</h2>
<ol type="1">
<li><p>User selects eligible objects and chooses Copy, Move, Delete or
Restore.</p></li>
<li><p>Client performs lightweight checks: selection limit, compatible
object store, destination required, obvious self/descendant
move.</p></li>
<li><p>Preview API returns estimate, warnings and a short-lived
validation token. Large previews may themselves run
asynchronously.</p></li>
<li><p>User confirms. ICN sends object IDs, operation, destination,
options and idempotency key—not credentials—to the plug-in
service.</p></li>
<li><p>Server authenticates current ICN identity, performs authoritative
authorization checks and creates BulkRequest in PENDING.</p></li>
<li><p>Bulk Action API registers the job durably and returns 202
Accepted with requestId, status URL and dashboard deep link.</p></li>
<li><p>ICN shows a non-blocking banner and releases the UI.
Reconciliation advances any stranded PENDING request.</p></li>
</ol>
<h2 id="worker-flow">5.2 Worker flow</h2>
<ol start="8" type="1">
<li><p>Worker atomically claims one QUEUED request in FileNet and sets
RUNNING, ExecutionNode, LeaseUntil and heartbeat.</p></li>
<li><p>Worker revalidates request ownership, repository access and
destination.</p></li>
<li><p>Enumerator walks the hierarchy using paged queries and compact
checkpoints; it never materializes the whole tree.</p></li>
<li><p>Processors handle bounded batches and check whether the requested
outcome already exists before applying a side effect.</p></li>
<li><p>After a completed batch, the worker saves counters,
LastCompletedBatch and any traversal token to BulkRequest or an optional
BulkRequestBatch child.</p></li>
<li><p>Heartbeat and LeaseUntil are renewed periodically; progress
updates are coalesced to protect FileNet.</p></li>
<li><p>Transient failures use bounded backoff. Permanent item failures
are written to the error report and processing continues according to
policy.</p></li>
<li><p>At the end, counters are reconciled and the FileNet request is
marked COMPLETED, PARTIAL_SUCCESS, FAILED or CANCELLED.</p></li>
</ol>
<h2 id="crash-recovery">5.3 Crash recovery</h2>
<p>If a worker stops renewing its FileNet lease, the recovery scheduler
may reclaim it after LeaseUntil expires. The replacement resumes from
the last committed batch/traversal checkpoint. Exactly-once execution is
not assumed; correctness comes from safe re-execution, idempotent
outcome checks and deterministic conflict rules.</p>
<h1 id="operation-semantics">6. Operation semantics</h1>
<table>
<colgroup>
<col style="width: 25%" />
<col style="width: 25%" />
<col style="width: 25%" />
<col style="width: 25%" />
</colgroup>
<thead>
<tr class="header">
<th><strong>Operation</strong></th>
<th><strong>Execution unit</strong></th>
<th><strong>Key validation</strong></th>
<th><strong>Idempotent/no-op rule</strong></th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr class="odd">
<td>COPY</td>
<td>One source object to one resolved target location</td>
<td>Read source; create/file target; class/property permissions;
destination capacity</td>
<td>If a correlated/equivalent target already exists and matches, mark
succeeded/no-op.</td>
</tr>
<tr class="even">
<td>MOVE</td>
<td>One filing/reference or folder edge, depending agreed semantics</td>
<td>Read source; file destination; unfile source; no move into
descendant</td>
<td>If already at destination and absent from source as required, mark
succeeded.</td>
</tr>
<tr class="odd">
<td>DELETE</td>
<td>One recoverable object or filing</td>
<td>Delete rights; retention/hold; checked-out/reservation rules</td>
<td>If already deleted/unfiled in intended mode, mark
succeeded/no-op.</td>
</tr>
<tr class="even">
<td>RESTORE</td>
<td>One recoverable object to original/fallback location</td>
<td>Recoverability; original destination exists; naming conflict;
permissions</td>
<td>If active object is already restored to intended location, mark
succeeded/no-op.</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<h2 id="folder-ordering">6.1 Folder ordering</h2>
<ul>
<li><p>Copy: create destination folder parent before children, then copy
documents/filings.</p></li>
<li><p>Move: validate the full topology first; process children/filings
in an order consistent with FileNet filing semantics.</p></li>
<li><p>Delete: process children before parent when the API or business
rule requires an empty folder.</p></li>
<li><p>Restore: restore parents before children; use a configured
fallback folder if the original parent no longer exists.</p></li>
</ul>
