<h1 id="security-and-authorization">7. Security and authorization</h1>
<ul>
<li><p>Run by user context where feasible. If a service account performs
repository calls, the orchestrator must enforce the initiating user’s
effective permissions before each operation; a privileged service
account must never silently expand authority.</p></li>
<li><p>Store stable user ID, display name and submitted security context
snapshot for audit. Never store a password or reusable user token in
BulkRequest.</p></li>
<li><p>Normal users may read only their own request objects. Admin
visibility is authorized server-side by configured groups/users; hiding
rows in JavaScript is insufficient.</p></li>
<li><p>Revalidate destination and object rights during execution because
ACLs, holds, filing and object state may change after
submission.</p></li>
<li><p>Restrict permanent-delete/purge, admin cancel, global retry and
priority changes to specific roles.</p></li>
<li><p>Sanitize StatusMessage and error exports to avoid leaking titles,
paths or exception stacks to users without object access.</p></li>
</ul>
<h2 id="filenet-security-model">7.1 FileNet security model</h2>
<p>Create request instances with an ACL that grants the submitter read
access, the worker service account update access, and configured bulk
administrators read/control access. Prefer security
proxies/marking-compatible rules only if already governed in the
repository. Query predicates improve performance but do not replace
object-level security.</p>
