<h2 id="refresh-strategy">9.4 Refresh strategy</h2>
<p>Use 10–15 second polling only while visible requests are
non-terminal, stop polling on hidden tabs, and apply jitter.
WebSocket/SSE is optional later; polling is simpler and sufficient
because FileNet progress is intentionally coalesced. Provide a manual
Refresh button and display “last updated.”</p>
<h1 id="progress-calculation-and-counters">10. Progress calculation and
counters</h1>
<p>Folder enumeration can change the denominator. Use phase-aware
progress: during DISCOVERING show an indeterminate bar and discovered
count; once enumeration freezes PlannedItemCount, compute processing
progress. For combined display, optionally reserve 10% for enumeration
and 90% for execution, but label the phase so the number is not
misleading.</p>
<table>
<colgroup>
<col style="width: 50%" />
<col style="width: 50%" />
</colgroup>
<thead>
<tr class="header">
<th><strong>Metric</strong></th>
<th><strong>Definition</strong></th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr class="odd">
<td>PlannedItemCount</td>
<td>Frozen count of executable items after discovery/enumeration.</td>
</tr>
<tr class="even">
<td>ProcessedCount</td>
<td>Succeeded + Failed + Skipped + Cancelled-item outcomes that are
terminal.</td>
</tr>
<tr class="odd">
<td>ProgressPercent</td>
<td>floor(100 × ProcessedCount / PlannedItemCount); terminal request is
forced to 100.</td>
</tr>
<tr class="even">
<td>CurrentRate</td>
<td>Recent processed items per minute, smoothed.</td>
</tr>
<tr class="odd">
<td>ETA</td>
<td>Shown only after sufficient stable samples; otherwise
“Calculating…”</td>
</tr>
<tr class="even">
<td>EstimatedItemCount</td>
<td>Preview estimate; never used as final denominator after plan
freeze.</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p>For streaming enumeration/execution overlap, track phase and
discovered counts separately. Do not let the visible percentage move
backwards; freeze the denominator before publishing a determinate
execution percentage or use a weighted two-phase model.</p>
